  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the React Application**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in designing the application within React, targeting a highly interactive and elegant user experience. I\'m focusing on incorporating beautiful UI elements that match the mockup and supporting all requested features with exceptional finesse. I\'m aiming for supreme elegance.\n\n\n**Refining the UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating dark mode, smooth transitions, and custom animations, specifically using `motion/react` for elegant visual flow. I\'m carefully inspecting the mockup structure, especially the nav bar and hero section, to build the React components with precision and create a responsive design. I\'m focusing on those micro-interactions!\n\n\n**Crafting the Hero Section**\n\nI\'m now implementing the Hero section, aiming for a luxurious and authoritative feel. I\'m focusing on the \"Illuminate Your Brand\" and \"View Portfolio\" buttons, giving them distinct aesthetics using gold and violet hues, with scaling and hover effects. The dynamic \"Luminous Orb\" background is next, a mouse-parallax effect for desktop and an animation on mobile, pulsing soft gold and violet. I\'ll finish with the animated scroll-down chevron. I\'m excited about this.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Designing the \"Origin Story\"**\n\nI\'m now building the \"Origin Story\" section. I\'m setting up a responsive side-by-side grid, displaying the Rayoba Media brand mark with a floating shadow effect. I\'ll begin with the logo card on the left side, carefully incorporating the given Rayoba logo. I\'m aiming for a visually appealing layout that tells a compelling story.\n\n\n**Constructing the Brand Narrative**\n\nI\'m now implementing the right side of the \"Origin Story\". I\'m incorporating the \"ORIGIN STORY\" badge, heading, and text, with a responsive layout. I\'m focusing on the interactive trivia feature for key words like \"Ray\" and \"Oba,\" using high-end interactive trivia cards. Finally, I\'ll add the \"ESTABLISHED IN EXCELLENCE\" footer with a golden separator line.\n\n\n**Building the Royal Arsenal**\n\nI\'m now deep in building the \"Royal Arsenal\" or \"Royal Services\" section, which will contain comprehensive digital solutions as the centerpiece of my app. I\'m focusing on the Bento grid layout, adjusting for both desktop and mobile views. I\'m working on the design of the cards with their distinct visual styles, including gilded and deep violet backgrounds, alongside dynamic content. I\'m now integrating an interactive slide-over or sleek detail overlay for each service, showing specific methodologies and deliverables.\n\n\n**Integrating Case Study Snippets**\n\nI\'m now integrating case study snippets and estimations into the \"Featured Work\" section! I\'m adding \"Legacy of Light\" as a scrollytelling component and enhancing the existing featured projects with detailed case studies. I\'m excited by this! I\'m aiming for full functionality! I\'ll include an interactive slider to show \"before\" and \"after\".\n\n\n**Developing the Estimation Tool**\n\nI\'m now implementing the interactive \"Brand Sovereign Assessment\" tool. Users can select their brand\'s stature, primary channels, and vision, which updates a dynamic \"Royalty Scope Estimation Summary\" in real-time. This also includes animated visuals and an option for a printable PDF, all client-side.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Application**\n\nI\'m now integrating the final touch points: I\'ve added the \"Ready to Illuminate Your Brand?\" subtitle with the magnetic hover button, ready to build the user\'s legacy. The footer is also nearly complete, with the \"Rayoba\" logo, link columns, and copyright text, ready for final review. I\'m excited by this. Now, I\'m focusing on the cinematic film grain overlay, glowing gradients, and dark/light mode toggle. A beautiful and modular React setup is underway, with carefully considered component and type structures.\n\n\n**Structuring the React Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the application\'s core structure. I\'m building out individual React components, starting with the `Navbar` to manage responsiveness and the dark/light mode toggle via state callbacks. I\'m working next on `Hero` with its dynamic parallax and smooth scroll triggers. I\'m then implementing `OriginStory`, which includes interactive modals and `BentoServices` to provide service details.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 12
      nanos: 161734556
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
