    summary: "Tailwind CSS v4 adopts a \"CSS-first\" approach for dark mode, moving configuration directly into your CSS files and eliminating the need for `tailwind.config.js` for this purpose[1][2][3][4]. To implement manual dark mode, you define a custom variant using the `@custom-variant` directive.\n\nHere\'s how to achieve manual dark mode in Tailwind CSS v4:\n\n1.  **Define a custom dark variant in your CSS:**\n    You will use the `@custom-variant` directive to tell Tailwind CSS when to apply the `dark:` styles. A common approach is to look for a `.dark` class on a parent element (like `<html>` or `<body>`). Add this to your main CSS file (e.g., `index.css` or `app.css`):\n\n    \n\nSources:\n[1] [tailkits.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFg3GP_3UJoTUeF2FBPXiJjvvMA4rPkeLdQKgYpp3Pqrz9Qm25XOIXqB9JQo4mq3mwuPpgrIXByW47pFt-mrF6z4VSh4QMo3nitwO-Kei3hfD3R53sl3cAoWnso8IRFrwxjbuCX5llgRkWOJYy0-dfPlBk=)\n[2] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFVkJ9VKeCuReRW1hg4H9iRhc0b3xZ5ZAwPVrYXLa6OLI8j1bBzo_AsLgUz0Lts4uNL5vYTWnj0S81dYTbdVnLMM3HytYoAV8PShXXLXeLuGLUW_KPFKr8BsJkz2z98Vj0bOW0HggFvyYGPS-Tvpq6rDfeqjklZz50ldbFS9kHYWP-JmpJzdVbLUosfwtCGhHUMTQuiuaNCnd0A3XgXz9djM6jm)\n[3] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHoam2V1vBhMFfPCcBWbCBg-kcmEx96Wjz4IiZNbpx5DVdIO0uJCl23Fr-VKzVUawDFvX_G7PPEBLukvyB4tlJi96-8cc8wml0lRSmLhmap18BgXNDq91VQBNlFKS-_Xc-xnjC2iqaQtyePiPcVT56xl8KCICEYy5cIGcmXSZ5gx-N3PmlwSSnw3kPz2vfAK_-dXCb0vPn_)\n[4] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEeHrUYtIcvV85hiKuCbZidqwmMeaA6uy5k8PloQYmuELzJwjtY3aJVIY6at7oiqDjReTCVZQVVbLKyA79GlOg9Z1s5st50C9cSlAIk5osdE3R6PDxHkjekYEz5ELuGuIYkMQPcZB5Mb0LoN7MGXILaB_2pUuASeBqS0lIuMxHj7J5dhUZLssdkloHcrOzEUDRmoOlgfCwduzr7ZqDODHj14Py6zaLdYLLb)\n[5] [tailadmin.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlIGlAQMUB9YAA0nMy7FE_jyYuYSZHfx9wQX