  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Discovering Dark Mode Toggles**\n\nI\'ve made a discovery! It looks like Tailwind v4 offers manual dark mode toggling, configured directly within the CSS. The key seems to be the `@variant dark` directive, paired with the `&:where(.dark, .dark *)` selector. This selector, particularly the `where()` part, is intriguing. It\'s becoming clearer.\n\n\n**Confirming Dark Mode Options**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that Tailwind v4 defaults to `prefers-color-scheme` for dark mode. For class-based toggling, `@variant dark (.dark &);` is the ticket. It\'s clean and efficient! I\'m now checking the existing `src/index.css` to confirm my understanding before testing with a compile or lint. Looking into the navbar component next to see how the toggle might be implemented.\n\n\n**Analyzing Dark Mode Implementation**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implementation. Examining `Navbar.tsx`, I see the `dark` class is applied directly to `document.documentElement`, synchronized with localStorage. This is similar in `App.tsx` where I see classes such as `dark:bg-midnight-royal`. I am now working through the implications. I\'m wondering if Tailwind v4 automatically handles dark mode based on the `dark:` classes, and I\'m looking at the implications of the configuration.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 173707424
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
