      title: "stackoverflow.com"
    }
    summary: "In Tailwind CSS v4, the `@variant dark` directive is used within a CSS-first configuration to manage dark mode styles, particularly when working with CSS variables[1][2][3]. This approach allows for defining custom colors and other styles that automatically switch based on the activated theme without needing to prefix every utility class with `dark:`[1].\n\nHere\'s how `@variant dark` is typically utilized:\n*   **CSS-First Configuration**: Tailwind CSS v4 promotes a CSS-first configuration, where styling and theme definitions, including dark mode, are primarily managed in your main CSS file. The `@variant dark` directive is a core part of this system[2].\n*   **Custom Dark Mode Detection**: You can define how the `dark` variant is activated. This often involves checking for a `.dark` class on the `<html>` element or a `data-theme=\"dark\"` attribute[3]. For instance:\n    \n\nSources:\n[1] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGnFnKY1JEFNEE3G065OEbBf_I8AhlDKSIlcfgOIZ34OL1uXzej4Vh7y4KEaIWbUCNoFod1iVtVctl47bZuMkeD1FDGvX8LcQHJ3IDqqZKAwwKeHAC510anE4RomuO39FQCONkn-SNrL0i_u5Nt_002NkP18eUoyBu3u3OTqBds-s6J53TO4Jl5D3SdhD3Pim6kx60_ou3cJeferI3JlrVaHMiucV1OPMKRABX87IrL1jVcflmeZA==)\n[2] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGUZMo202kql6UXzUNUrHMTqiszoavF_dwE6c4UlWDyTA8mssMrbvvA2G_Y-Ju3vMx4g2VjLfG-PoAZe5e3P_WuJSqCQpTEBzU8rx4Vc0-92DsMs_rdOFqf3oiqDmaGoZfob_dqVYkVgPFZzAyadvPsrYNxqZ5utWEyzkeRHR7wyVemyhhpMH306Nx8yc9JGxq4RLVDw8FglRnLhoxC_Ak9XvNYdQ==)\n[3] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGArUXZvoGCpmCQqk_CKgjyObmM0VSvfnBUV7BlCLAbI8tChyTsDdIevWLjx4f5O3VEYHQhdE0-HZDt_T5YEbi1BG1d2Z07PIcub3tJgMs-fIgKDtIu69POTqYQLRrUnToaVomLoDJvby0dcaLA9jGSf4Y22q7Bqk4=)\n[4] [hbui.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQELMmFI7hdPG4nUJarKCW0r6MEr2D0l3YFKxM-8CdwhaFAJhU5IF6M827hvMlcNeAl_1yoXie-QuXUOkfUCtaGQxXWehKbGC8-b