    web_documents {
      url: "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFZHuo9sKOHG0e0cIXk_YUTzT3nkkYUOGrv1stLQ04VVp9uRv3HI326JN5Qr_8ziatXBAjwYhI_o1OxVI-yY9dg59MVzdN10uWsY4yROQYva4T0zxMEMC1yXNr6Fi-9XrqKtq_BvQ41ZceHxCWlJGoQrc5eY1kRkA6DNJRcPkV2yj_w2IUDRrGqUrDSqQbAgTrfXi8="
      title: "kitemetric.com"
    }
    summary: "Tailwind CSS v4 significantly changes how manual dark mode is implemented, shifting towards a CSS-first configuration rather than relying on a JavaScript configuration file. The core of this functionality lies in the `@variant dark` directive within your main CSS file, allowing you to define a custom selector that triggers dark mode styles.[1][2][3]\n\nHere\'s how to set up manual dark mode using `@variant dark` in Tailwind CSS v4:\n\n**1. Configure the `@variant dark` directive in your CSS:**\nInstead of a `darkMode` key in `tailwind.config.js` (as in v3), you now define the dark variant directly in your main CSS file (e.g., `index.css` or `app.css`). This directive tells Tailwind which CSS selector should activate dark mode.\n\n*   **Using a `data-theme=\"dark\"` attribute:**\n    To activate dark mode when the `<html>` or `<body>` element has a `data-theme=\"dark\"` attribute, you would use:\n    \n\nSources:\n[1] [thingsaboutweb.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEl0qkZwPld2uKhreFXfGbRDlixUl-Z2haSmjClsyY4uzgGVtRreAE5zKCxC1VVUFCVoYRuaHd7U7vRv37Ik8ZqF5vHtFKJuqi40CC3zdqyu3JAbE8m7Y6LV0br3qiAsXtczq_kshX1pbFPDWx5Nn5z6IIJJFU42B2C1P3iQVtqRpNWJQ==)\n[2] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGJOyoEqqBa8u7T2J0CnGTzbHilguOjyqdWzm46afy0p3kAds5DSXhfbO7UJZ8lRS5cYjCLB59nyKTSOQPB1qfaWcXYWy4jgTSUYrECxr_Tqahe2L5IK_AjvLJTaqK28OpEuCjbMYuch3dTsZtEqxhm9jYNu3FNTD0aT8htIMyIk3K4EsgkJO-7TqxXlUkUmngkR7NV05oxqPleF8h5lF6Q1--_)\n[3] [tailkits.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFMTGXaNeYrv_U-T5UFhpqYnP5BWMaff0wm3mM7J3cBVnL4Zr8VTi4iYLliXgz9PFMHbpwjBtkVpdRBBhCexzBHe_dp-DN4XNW3obR3XxNHQtFnoE-KtqSQGoKfj03EbDdb55RJ46FuPEa5mjc9gT-Mppw=)\n[4] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFsNZyCnjpHwfSv1m0mGtF7rvaNTkT9LvEe9P47XIi2GxCIkYsd3ECM5QYyE5f06B-M0YVpv0iPxYakSmqxFIBITQo2aFzB6USc0ZJmaZtnAdqHLNWGaPwG8IvUeQILe7X2L0eSRJzoVARDcqGI4ZIFbSzMVbI6Dw==)\n[5] [dev.to](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFbF6SseWh5u1CaqA_qR8MBTyp-IC8iVIQ_PjcM9KLEPLwJ1Zt92dFe84cVKjPev7hUMQKUpSRT64dZr1yNmWxI1zaNt9-TZCE227n5FoYbcJVgSuQflAiceBJ8DhkPXrmpRaZqqqQCpcJqo2wQJbD61dWo_X3qzbjz8x4vau7IoVoT)\n[6] [dev.to](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHkwn_N4pM0lndh0tUk_EkZ0-WZdDHW-vZuG6Kbc7zwTBs5gU4uulk4W4g6AN3hH6XlvaqRpbzAIWn1DuwLs0TxXpE9utww6-p8gAA4pZyRty7GGeJUOmXvgSffpKaMMg_60dDxCUpmMZFrHLshqaEIO0A=)\n[7] [preline.co](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHLOjnx3ZdAH6AOHwYCf9izYE35tgsC9GVhn6vZlClGb76sDO2aMeXz6wUswrxg54XwpMOvDhOLQZJEQSVkVLlR87ZeYopnD-yr9y-bXyHWHB1jQNxAXuzvjDwWsG1CN6Q=)\n[8] [kitemetric.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFZHuo9sKOHG0e0cIXk_YUTzT3nkkYUOGrv1stLQ04VVp9uRv3HI326JN5Qr_8ziatXBAjwYhI_o1OxVI-yY9dg59MVzdN10uWsY4yROQYva4T0zxMEMC1yXNr6Fi-9XrqKtq_BvQ41ZceHxCWlJGoQrc5eY1kRkA6DNJRcPkV2yj_w2IUDRrGqUrDSqQbAgTrfXi8=)"
