    thinking: "**Verifying Exquisite Contrast**\n\nI\'ve achieved a fully clean linter, which is wonderful! Now, I\'m focusing on refining the light and dark mode transition. My current thought is to verify that the contrast in the body and overall text is absolutely exquisite in light mode, with the background set to `bg-off`.\n\n\n**Assessing Page Readability**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the individual pages, ensuring consistent readability and visual appeal. For the portfolio page, light mode uses `bg-gray-50` with dark text, while dark mode employs `dark:bg-black/30`. I\'m verifying the contrast is optimal across all elements. Also checking Email marketing background, which is `bg-royal-gold` with `text-deep-violet` text, it is high-contrast.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have successfully completed your request to make the manual dark mode toggle functional and introduced a highly coordinated light theme palette that matches the luxury branding and editorial style of **Rayoba Media**.\n\n### \360\237\233\240\357\270\217 What has been implemented:\n\n1. **Tailwind CSS v4 Manual Selector Activation**:\n   - Integrated the manual class directive directly within `src/index.css` using Tailwind v4 custom variants:\n     ```css\n     @variant dark (&:where(.dark, .dark *));\n     ```\n   - This explicitly instructs Tailwind\'s compiler to map the `.dark` class toggled on the `html` root node directly to modern stylesheet classes, rather than relying exclusively on system media queries.\n\n2. **Liquid Transition Flow & Backdrop Harmonization**:\n   - Defined precise global backgrounds on the root `html` and `body` nodes:\n     - **Ivory Mode**: Cozy, custom warm-tinted ivory off-white background (`#fcf8f9`).\n     - **Midnight Mode**: Deep blackish midnight sapphire/royal background (`#0A0A0B`).\n   - Configured high-contrast copy colors (`text-gray-800` vs. `var(--color-gilded-ivory)`) to secure strict readability standards.\n   - Built an ease-out background and color transition delay to ensure that flipping between themes is visually premium, fluid, and free of jagged flickering.\n\n3. **Background Luminous Orb Blend Controls**:\n   - Altered the background glowing interactive orb in `Hero.tsx`. In light mode, using *screen blend* would wash out completely on white. We implemented a dynamic multi-variant transition:\n     ```tsx\n     className=\"... mix-blend-multiply dark:mix-blend-screen opacity-15 dark:opacity-40\"\n     ```\n   - This renders a soft, elegant golden-shadow halo in light mode and transforms into a vibrant, modern gilded nebula in dark mode.\n\n4. **Linter & Compiler Validation**:\n   - Ran extensive type safety checks and confirmed that the application compiles without any warnings or syntax errors."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 914809044
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
