    thinking: "**Analyzing Hero Component Animation**\n\nI\'ve been looking closely at the animation implementation within the `Hero` component, specifically focusing on the `motion.div` element in `/src/components/Hero.tsx`. The initial state, animation target, and transition duration are defined; I\'m trying to refine how these are configured to improve performance and user experience. I\'ll need to consider how the motion properties affect overall layout.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Hierarchy**\n\nI\'m now considering the visual hierarchy, spurred by the request to remove the text \"Editorial Design & Brand Dominance.\" This prompted an examination of where that content should go, and if the current Hero section layout is the best. The idea is to move the content to the top of the initial screen, with the animated circle and logo centered. I\'m focusing on the Hero section on the homepage.\n\n\n**Integrating New Visuals**\n\nI\'m now integrating the new visuals, specifically the \"RayOba Coat of Arms\" card, at the top of the first page. I\'m focusing on incorporating the animated circle with the crown, text \"Ray (Light) x Oba (King)\" and the detailed description, ensuring the content flows logically. The square shape will likely be smaller, placed at the top of the hero component, above the headline. The Rayoba crown logo will be centered inside.\n\n\n**Revising Content Placement**\n\nI\'m now revising the content placement within the `Hero` section. My focus is on removing the \"Editorial Design & Brand Dominance\" badge and incorporating the new \"Ray (Light) x Oba (King)\" text and description. I\'m exploring how to best position these elements, keeping the animated circle with the crown logo centered, and the text above the visuals. This includes rethinking the square shape, and refining the placement of the content in the `Hero.tsx` component.\n\n\n"
